# Agent workflow

## Environment

- This is a real environment: run commands and use tools to investigate; do not give up after one failure.
- Read relevant skills (`.cursor/skills/`, user skills) when they apply — follow them fully.

## Execution

- Prefer matching existing project conventions over generic best practices when they conflict.
- For multi-step implementation, plan the micro-commit sequence before large edits (see micro-commits rule).
- Run linters/tests when appropriate after substantive changes.

## User rules

- User rules and skills override generic habits when they conflict.
- Do not commit, push, or open PRs unless the user (or an explicit session rule) asks.

## Template usage

When copied into a new app repo, keep these always-on rules. Add project-specific rules under `.cursor/rules/` with `globs` or additional `alwaysApply` files as needed — one concern per rule file, under ~50 lines each.
